1
00:00:21,897 --> 00:00:23,899
[ III ]

2
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:33,951
NARRATOR : I busied myself to think of a story

3
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:38,497
which would speak to the mysterious fears of our nature

4
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:42,960
and awaken thrilling horror .

5
00:00:43,126 --> 00:00:48,474
One to make the reader dread to look around .

6
00:00:48,632 --> 00:00:53,763
To curdle the blood , and quicken the beatings of the heart .

7
00:00:53,929 --> 00:00:55,931
[ III ]

8
00:01:44,396 --> 00:01:45,898
[ GRUNTING ]

9
00:01:46,064 --> 00:01:51,036
SAILOR 1 : Tell the captain , we 've got to take in the topsail .

10
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:53,788
She 's going to rip !

11
00:01:58,327 --> 00:02:02,753
Please , captain ! We have to drop the sails !

12
00:02:02,914 --> 00:02:04,882
All hands to the mast !

13
00:02:05,042 --> 00:02:07,170
Take the wheel ! Come on !

14
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:16,061
SAILOR 1 : Captain , we 've hit the ice ! We 've hit the ice !

15
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:19,223
Iceberg ahead !

16
00:02:24,603 --> 00:02:26,571
Hard to starboard !

17
00:02:31,735 --> 00:02:33,203
SAILOR 2 : Go back !

18
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:45,419
[ SCREAMING ]

19
00:02:53,632 --> 00:02:55,600
Help ! Help !

20
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:59,934
Help ! Hold on , Vernon !

21
00:03:01,223 --> 00:03:02,440
Hold on !

22
00:03:23,787 --> 00:03:26,961
WALTON : Put your backs into it , men !

23
00:03:27,791 --> 00:03:28,838
Let 's go !

24
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,844
Captain , this is useless . The ice stretches for miles .

25
00:03:32,003 --> 00:03:34,301
What do you suggest we do ? Lay down and die ?

26
00:03:34,464 --> 00:03:37,092
The men are exhausted , sir . They can 't go on , man .

27
00:03:37,259 --> 00:03:40,684
I tell you , I have not come this far to give up now .

28
00:03:41,263 --> 00:03:43,311
They knew the risk when they signed on .

29
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:46,818
And we are gonna chop our way to the North Pole if we have to .

30
00:03:46,977 --> 00:03:50,322
Then you run the risk of mutiny , captain .

31
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:54,526
Did you say mutiny ? Yes I did , sir .

32
00:03:56,820 --> 00:04:01,826
We proceed north as planned .

33
00:04:02,659 --> 00:04:04,627
At the cost of how many more lives ?

34
00:04:04,786 --> 00:04:07,335
As many as it takes !

35
00:04:10,834 --> 00:04:12,836
[ CREATURE HOWLS ]

36
00:04:18,842 --> 00:04:20,185
[ BARKING ]

37
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:23,513
There 's something out there .

38
00:04:24,598 --> 00:04:26,350
