87
00:07:56,393 --> 00:07:59,067
MRS. MORITZ : Madam ! You will spoil the boy , really .

88
00:08:08,196 --> 00:08:10,540
FATHER : Would you and your daughter leave us , please , Mrs. Moritz ?

89
00:08:10,699 --> 00:08:11,746
Doctor .

90
00:08:13,785 --> 00:08:15,082
Come along , Justine .

91
00:08:17,414 --> 00:08:22,466
Victor , this is Elizabeth . She 's coming to live with us .

92
00:08:22,669 --> 00:08:28,927
She 's lost both her mother and father to the scarlet fever , Victor .

93
00:08:29,092 --> 00:08:30,935
She 's an orphan now .

94
00:08:31,094 --> 00:08:33,062
You must think of her as your own sister .

95
00:08:35,765 --> 00:08:40,066
You must look after her , and be kind to her .

96
00:08:42,814 --> 00:08:44,441
Always .

97
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:46,530
[ III ]

98
00:08:57,579 --> 00:09:01,129
Mother , oh . How is the imminent arrival ?

99
00:09:01,291 --> 00:09:04,010
Oh , a little frisky today . Yes .

100
00:09:13,303 --> 00:09:16,682
When you were a little boy , you used to chase fireflies in the field .

101
00:09:16,848 --> 00:09:19,317
Yes , and when I trapped them in my jar , they died .

102
00:09:19,476 --> 00:09:20,978
Yes . And do you remember how you cried ?

103
00:09:21,144 --> 00:09:23,272
Yes . Because you wanted to keep them

104
00:09:23,438 --> 00:09:24,940
