150
00:12:43,054 --> 00:12:45,022
Oh , Mother .

151
00:12:45,682 --> 00:12:51,189
You should never have died . No one need ever die .

152
00:12:51,854 --> 00:12:54,357
I will stop this .

153
00:12:55,525 --> 00:12:57,653
I will stop this .

154
00:12:58,361 --> 00:13:00,363
I promise .

155
00:13:01,322 --> 00:13:05,247
ELIZABETH : Victor , you 're completely obsessed . Please explain what that is .

156
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:08,250
VICTOR : It 's energy . It never disappears , it merely changes form .

157
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:10,502
It 's possible to convert this candle wax

158
00:13:10,665 --> 00:13:12,838
into the convulsions of a mechanical dog .

159
00:13:13,001 --> 00:13:17,723
But the applications of this are limitless . Really .

160
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:21,430
Oh , please come outside , Victor . It 's such a beautiful day .

161
00:13:21,592 --> 00:13:23,970
Go away , I 'm busy .

162
00:13:27,765 --> 00:13:29,859
What 's this ?

163
00:13:30,393 --> 00:13:32,987
It 's for spraying down the electric eels .

164
00:13:33,146 --> 00:13:34,398
[ LAUGHING ]

165
00:13:34,564 --> 00:13:37,864
Now , put it down . Put it down . It 's not for playing with .

166
00:13:38,026 --> 00:13:41,405
It 's not for playing with . Put it down , put it down- - Don 't do that .

167
00:13:41,571 --> 00:13:45,246
I warned you . Don 't- - Don 't- - Give me that , you little ...

168
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:50,122
VICTOR : Come on !

169
00:13:50,288 --> 00:13:52,290
[ ELIZABETH VICTOR SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY ]

170
00:13:54,792 --> 00:13:56,214
Yes ! Come on !

171
00:13:56,377 --> 00:13:58,095
After all , we should be grateful to Victor

172
00:13:58,254 --> 00:14:00,757
for abandoning his experiments for one afternoon .

173
00:14:00,923 --> 00:14:03,426
Well , who says I have ?

174
00:14:03,634 --> 00:14:04,681
What do you mean ?

175
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:05,891
[ THUNDER CRASHES ]

176
00:14:06,054 --> 00:14:08,603
Look ! ELIZABETH : We 're all going to die .

177
00:14:08,765 --> 00:14:10,938
You knew this was going to happen . No , not for certain .

178
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:12,522
But I had hoped the conditions would be right .

179
00:14:12,685 --> 00:14:14,312
They 're quite common here at this time of year .

180
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:16,898
I 've never seen one quite as large as that , though . Look .

181
00:14:17,065 --> 00:14:19,909
Isn 't it wonderful ? Victor , you shouldn 't have done this .

182
00:14:20,068 --> 00:14:21,570
It 's all right , it 's all right .

183
00:14:21,736 --> 00:14:23,204
We must take cover . A tree !

184
00:14:23,363 --> 00:14:25,161
No , no , no . That 's exactly the wrong thing to do .

185
00:14:25,323 --> 00:14:27,121
It 's potentially a much larger conductor than we are .

186
00:14:27,283 --> 00:14:28,956
Victor , what about Willie ? Um ...

187
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:31,917
What are we to do ? Come on .

188
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:34,833
VICTOR : Now , everyone , spread out . Elizabeth , take this . Now , quickly .

189
00:14:35,458 --> 00:14:38,177
Come on , quickly ! ELIZABETH : What is that ?

190
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:41,130
VICTOR : Dig it right into the ground . Go ahead .

191
00:14:41,297 --> 00:14:43,470
ELIZABETH : Now what ? VICTOR : Justine , take this . Come on .

192
00:14:43,633 --> 00:14:46,477
JUSTINE : Willie ! VICTOR : Everyone down .

193
00:14:46,636 --> 00:14:47,683
[ LAUGHING ]

194
00:14:47,845 --> 00:14:51,691
VICTOR : Give me your hands . It 'll be fine . Now take him . Now , that 's good .

195
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:53,567
ELIZABETH : Victor , I hope you know what you 're doing .

196
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:55,399
VICTOR : Willie ? Willie , don 't look up !

197
00:14:55,561 --> 00:14:56,938
Willie . Victor- -

198
00:14:57,105 --> 00:15:01,360
Wait ! One , two , three ...

199
00:15:08,241 --> 00:15:10,243
[ III ]

200
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:12,833
Now .

201
00:15:12,995 --> 00:15:15,589
[ ELECTRICITY CRACKLING ]

202
00:15:28,386 --> 00:15:31,230
VICTOR : So how do you feel , Elizabeth ?

203
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:34,855
ELIZABETH : Alive .

204
00:15:35,685 --> 00:15:37,687
[ CLASSICAL MUSIC PLAYING ]

205
00:15:37,895 --> 00:15:39,897
[ LAUGHING ]

206
00:16:05,173 --> 00:16:09,644
Ladies and gentlemen , dear friends . Gather round and listen .

207
00:16:10,178 --> 00:16:13,728
As you probably know , tomorrow my dear son Victor

208
00:16:13,890 --> 00:16:16,609
leaves me to pursue , what I 'm sure

209
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:19,236
will be an illustrious career in a profession

210
00:16:19,395 --> 00:16:21,443
I , myself , am not altogether unassociated with .

211
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:23,490
Ha , ha . Oh , modesty .

212
00:16:23,649 --> 00:16:25,242
[ LAUGHING ]

213
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:31,249
No . My - My- - My one regret is that his mother

214
00:16:32,408 --> 00:16:37,084
my late wife , is not here

215
00:16:39,582 --> 00:16:43,382
to share the pride

216
00:16:45,254 --> 00:16:47,928
which our son fills me with tonight .

217
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:53,687
Yes .

218
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:01,729
She wanted you to have this , Victor .

219
00:17:01,896 --> 00:17:03,944
On your graduation .

220
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:08,744
And in it she has written :

221
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:14,621
" This is the journal of Victor Frankenstein . "

222
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:20,339
The rest of the leaves are blank ,

223
00:17:22,917 --> 00:17:26,091
to be filled with the deeds of a noble life .

224
00:17:28,548 --> 00:17:30,550
[ GUESTS CLAPPING ]

225
00:17:34,303 --> 00:17:36,305
[ CLASSICAL MUSIC PLAYING ]

226
00:17:51,862 --> 00:17:55,617
We 'd , uh , better go in , before they miss us .

227
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:58,161
Just a little while longer . Please .

228
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:02,798
I don 't know when we 'll be alone together again .

229
00:18:02,957 --> 00:18:04,755
[ LAUGHING ]

230
00:18:05,251 --> 00:18:06,468
Oh , dear Victor .

231
00:18:07,628 --> 00:18:09,471
I shall miss you laughing at me .

232
00:18:11,257 --> 00:18:13,680
I 'll miss you making me laugh .

233
00:18:21,684 --> 00:18:23,152
So ...

234
00:18:27,148 --> 00:18:29,867
how do brothers and sisters say goodbye ?

235
00:18:34,071 --> 00:18:35,698
Perhaps they never have to .

236
00:18:37,867 --> 00:18:39,540
I won 't , if you won 't .

237
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:44,498
[ III ]

238
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:57,679
Are you my sister ?

239
00:18:59,513 --> 00:19:01,231
Sister ...

240
00:19:01,849 --> 00:19:03,726
friend ...

241
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:06,612
lover .

242
00:19:08,606 --> 00:19:10,574
Wife ?

243
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,572
Yes .

244
00:19:12,735 --> 00:19:15,033
Then come with me to Ingolstadt . Marry me now .

245
00:19:15,196 --> 00:19:17,415
Victor , no . Well , then I 'll stay .

246
00:19:17,573 --> 00:19:18,665
Oh .

247
00:19:18,824 --> 00:19:23,580
I want more than anything else in the world to be your wife .

248
00:19:23,746 --> 00:19:27,341
But as long as you 're away , I belong here .

249
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:31,091
I want to make this house live again .

250
00:19:31,253 --> 00:19:35,258
I want to make this a great home for our children .

251
00:19:36,217 --> 00:19:40,643
And now you must go , and do the great things you need to do .

252
00:19:41,472 --> 00:19:43,895
I want you so much .

253
00:19:45,267 --> 00:19:47,986
I 'll be here when you return .

254
00:19:48,479 --> 00:19:53,155
Each holiday . Every visit .

255
00:19:57,446 --> 00:19:59,790
Then on our wedding night .

256
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,962
Until our wedding night .

257
00:20:19,135 --> 00:20:21,137
[ III ]

258
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:23,931
[ SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY ]

259
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:37,653
WOMAN : Lots of stairs , I 'm afraid .

260
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:38,912
How was your journey ?

261
00:20:39,071 --> 00:20:40,869
It was very good , thank you . I made very good progress

262
00:20:41,031 --> 00:20:42,999
over the mountains . Clear run . Good . I am pleased .

263
00:20:43,159 --> 00:20:46,504
Well , as I said , we 've only got attic space .

264
00:20:46,662 --> 00:20:48,164
VICTOR : It 's exactly what I 'm looking for .

265
00:20:48,330 --> 00:20:50,674
But Frau Brach , there will be a great deal

266
00:20:50,833 --> 00:20:53,461
of scientific equipment and rigging to be delivered .

267
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:56,676
Every day , I 'm afraid , for the next week . I trust you have no objections .

268
00:20:56,839 --> 00:21:00,184
I 'm sure you appreciate the need for a proper laboratory , madam .

269
00:21:00,342 --> 00:21:02,185
Oh , Putzi likes you .

270
00:21:03,846 --> 00:21:05,848
[ III ]

271
00:21:10,561 --> 00:21:12,563
This will be perfect .

272
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:20,572
MAN : " The foolish and vain force their views by the rod .

273
00:21:20,738 --> 00:21:25,164
But knowledge is power only through God . "

274
00:21:25,326 --> 00:21:30,708
Our motto . Easily forgotten by you young men in a hurry .

275
00:21:30,873 --> 00:21:32,921
[ LAUGHING ]

276
00:21:33,083 --> 00:21:39,432
But perhaps the greatest mistake that all students make

277
00:21:40,049 --> 00:21:43,553
during their time here , is to suppose

278
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:48,725
that they can ever have an original or creative thought .

279
00:21:50,392 --> 00:21:54,863
We have all imagined that in our time .

280
00:21:59,985 --> 00:22:04,741
But gentlemen , you have not come here in order to think for yourselves .

281
00:22:04,907 --> 00:22:09,754
You are here to learn how to think for your patients .

282
00:22:09,912 --> 00:22:12,711
You must learn , therefore , in the first place

283
00:22:12,873 --> 00:22:15,296
to submit yourselves

284
00:22:15,501 --> 00:22:20,428
to the established laws of physical reality .

285
00:22:20,589 --> 00:22:21,886
But surely , professor ,

286
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:26,937
you don 't intend we disregard more philosophical approaches ?

287
00:22:27,096 --> 00:22:28,439
Philosophical ?

288
00:22:29,557 --> 00:22:32,060
Those which stir the imagination as well as the intellect ,

289
00:22:32,226 --> 00:22:34,069
as in Paracelsus , for example .

290
00:22:34,228 --> 00:22:38,529
Ah , Paracelsus . An arrogant and foolish Swiss .

291
00:22:39,066 --> 00:22:40,283
Albertus Magnus ?

292
00:22:40,442 --> 00:22:45,414
His nonsense was exploded 500 years ago .

293
00:22:45,573 --> 00:22:47,291
Cornelius Agrippa ?

294
00:22:47,449 --> 00:22:50,453
A sorcerer . An occultist . What is your name ?

295
00:22:51,453 --> 00:22:55,253
Victor Frankenstein , sir . Of Geneva .

296
00:22:55,416 --> 00:22:56,633
[ STUDENTS CHUCKLE ]

297
00:22:56,792 --> 00:22:59,090
Oh-ho . Another Swiss .

298
00:22:59,253 --> 00:23:04,601
Mr. Frankenstein , here at the University of Ingolstadt , we teach- -

299
00:23:04,758 --> 00:23:07,682
And indeed , hope to advance . - -the science of medicine .

300
00:23:07,845 --> 00:23:12,271
Chemistry , biology , physics . We study hard science .

301
00:23:12,433 --> 00:23:16,279
Yeah , but surely , professor , the greatest possible advances lie in combining these things .

302
00:23:16,437 --> 00:23:19,486
We do not study the ravings of lunatics and alchemists

303
00:23:19,648 --> 00:23:22,322
hundreds of years in their graves

304
00:23:22,818 --> 00:23:28,120
because their kind of amateur , fanatical , fantastical speculation

305
00:23:28,282 --> 00:23:31,206
does not heal bodies or save lives .

306
00:23:31,368 --> 00:23:33,666
Only science can do that .

307
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:35,831
[ STUDENTS MURMUR AND APPLAUD ]

308
00:23:37,207 --> 00:23:42,088
Now , have we your permission to continue ?

309
00:23:42,254 --> 00:23:44,256
[ CHATTERING ]

310
00:23:45,174 --> 00:23:48,018
Nice coat . Why , thank you .

311
00:23:48,177 --> 00:23:49,349
Don 't take it too hard .

312
00:23:49,511 --> 00:23:51,684
It 's just that Krempe doesn 't approve of public humiliation .

313
00:23:51,847 --> 00:23:52,894
I am not mad !

314
00:23:53,057 --> 00:23:54,650
My dear fellow , of course you 're not .

315
00:23:54,808 --> 00:23:58,028
In fact , that 's just the sort of thing I 'd expect a perfectly rational person

316
00:23:58,187 --> 00:24:00,565
to say to a complete stranger .

317
00:24:00,731 --> 00:24:04,326
Henry Clerval , by the way , and I 'm completely crazy .

318
00:24:04,485 --> 00:24:06,362
Victor Frankenstein . Of Geneva .

319
00:24:06,528 --> 00:24:08,201
Of Geneva . Yes , I noti -

320
00:24:08,364 --> 00:24:10,867
Why don 't you look where I 'm going ?

321
00:24:12,701 --> 00:24:15,045
That 's Schiller . Ornement of the playmg field .

322
00:24:15,204 --> 00:24:16,547
Really . He 's new as well .

323
00:24:16,705 --> 00:24:20,255
You can tell because he goes around looking at things with his mouth open .

324
00:24:21,752 --> 00:24:23,720
What are you here for ?

325
00:24:24,505 --> 00:24:26,553
Research . Very grand .

326
00:24:26,715 --> 00:24:28,888
I 'm here to become a mere doctor .

327
00:24:29,051 --> 00:24:31,349
I 'm told it has something to do with healing the sick .

328
00:24:31,512 --> 00:24:34,857
Which is a pity , really , because I find sick people rather revolting .

329
00:24:35,015 --> 00:24:38,394
Still , I 'll have a good time , get my degree- -

330
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:40,358
If I can stop failing Anatomy .

331
00:24:40,521 --> 00:24:44,116
- -And settle down to relieve rich old ladies of their imaginary ailments

332
00:24:44,274 --> 00:24:47,369
and then relieve their very real and beautiful daughters .

333
00:24:47,528 --> 00:24:49,576
Who was that ? He was at the lecture .

334
00:24:49,738 --> 00:24:50,910
Ah . That 's Waldman .

335
00:24:51,073 --> 00:24:52,416
Ah , that 's Waldman . Yes .

336
00:24:52,574 --> 00:24:54,918
Interesting case . They say in his youth

337
00:24:55,077 --> 00:24:57,751
he could break into heaven and lecture God on science .

338
00:24:57,913 --> 00:25:00,257
Ran into trouble with the authorities a few years back .

339
00:25:00,416 --> 00:25:02,760
Something to do with illegal experiments .

340
00:25:02,918 --> 00:25:05,546
But what kind of experiments , I wonder ?

341
00:25:05,713 --> 00:25:07,715
So what was it you were saying ? Uh ...

342
00:25:07,881 --> 00:25:09,929
Rich old ladies and their daughters ?

343
00:25:10,092 --> 00:25:13,562
Yes , it 's a life of sacrifice , I know , but someone 's got to do it .

344
00:25:13,721 --> 00:25:14,938
[ BOTH CHUCKLE ]

345
00:25:15,097 --> 00:25:16,269
[ HORSE NEIGHS ]

346
00:25:16,432 --> 00:25:18,434
[ III ]

347
00:25:28,694 --> 00:25:31,163
WALDMAN : And that is why the central nervous system

348
00:25:31,321 --> 00:25:33,494
and its crowning achievement , the brain ,

349
00:25:33,699 --> 00:25:36,293
are as complicated and mysterious a set of organs

350
00:25:36,452 --> 00:25:38,671
as you are ever likely to encounter .

351
00:25:38,829 --> 00:25:42,800
Mr. Frankenstein , the incision is yours .

352
00:25:48,422 --> 00:25:49,969
Excellent .

353
00:25:50,132 --> 00:25:54,603
Mr. Clerval , you may remove the cranial lid .

354
00:25:58,307 --> 00:26:01,937
" Henry , now fully recovered , and continues his struggle to pass Anatomy . "

355
00:26:02,102 --> 00:26:03,695
I was always terrible at anatomy .

356
00:26:03,854 --> 00:26:05,822
" Professor Waldman is very tolerant of him , and of myself .

357
00:26:05,981 --> 00:26:07,324
I 'm learning a great deal . "

358
00:26:07,483 --> 00:26:10,202
Professor Waldman is remarkable . And so is Henry .

359
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:12,203
" God bless you , all my love , Victor . "

360
00:26:12,362 --> 00:26:14,535
That 's very nice . " P.S. I 've fallen in love . "

361
00:26:14,740 --> 00:26:16,037
I beg your pardon ?

362
00:26:16,241 --> 00:26:18,790
" She 's dark , sleek , and beautiful ,

363
00:26:18,952 --> 00:26:21,671
and always wags her tail whenever she sees me .

364
00:26:21,830 --> 00:26:25,801
Her name is Putzi , and she 's the friendliest sheepdog that I 've ever known . "

365
00:26:25,959 --> 00:26:28,838
[ LAUGHING ]

366
00:26:29,004 --> 00:26:33,350
" P.S. Elizabeth , I dream of how your hair shines ... "

367
00:26:33,509 --> 00:26:36,558
VICTOR : " Of how your lips taste . I dream of your arms and breasts

368
00:26:36,762 --> 00:26:41,313
and of the time on our wedding night when we will be atone together at last . "

369
00:26:41,475 --> 00:26:42,897
WILLIE : What else does it say ?

370
00:26:43,060 --> 00:26:46,189
It says , " I 'm working very hard to make lots of new friends . "

371
00:26:46,355 --> 00:26:48,153
More coffee , anyone ?

372
00:26:50,776 --> 00:26:57,034
Once and for all , Frankenstein ! Life is life , death is death .

373
00:26:57,533 --> 00:26:59,035
These things are real .

374
00:26:59,201 --> 00:27:01,875
They are absolute . That is rubbish and you know it !

375
00:27:02,037 --> 00:27:05,041
That premise has been repeatedly challenged by members on your own staff !

376
00:27:05,207 --> 00:27:08,177
Yes , you , sir ! We don 't know where life ends or death begins .

377
00:27:08,335 --> 00:27:12,056
Hair continues to grow after what we choose to call death . So do fingernails .

378
00:27:12,214 --> 00:27:14,342
We know that a man 's brain may die

379
00:27:14,508 --> 00:27:17,387
but his heart and lungs may continue to pump and breathe .

380
00:27:17,553 --> 00:27:18,770
Now , you know that .

381
00:27:18,929 --> 00:27:21,432
Mr. Frankenstein of Geneva , I warn you

382
00:27:21,598 --> 00:27:26,104
what you are suggesting is not only illegal , it is immoral .

383
00:27:26,311 --> 00:27:27,813
Rubbish !

384
00:27:29,523 --> 00:27:33,278
" Dear diary , why does no one understand me ?

385
00:27:33,443 --> 00:27:35,696
P.S. I am not mad . "

386
00:27:36,613 --> 00:27:38,081
WALDMAN : You .

387
00:27:39,116 --> 00:27:41,585
Explain yourself . Professor , I 'm sorry .

388
00:27:41,743 --> 00:27:44,417
Listen , I came here to learn all about the new science .

389
00:27:44,580 --> 00:27:46,628
About galvanism , Franklin 's experiments .

390
00:27:46,832 --> 00:27:48,550
The combination of modern disciplines with ancient knowledge

391
00:27:48,709 --> 00:27:52,088
in an attempt to protect and create- - To create what ?

392
00:27:54,047 --> 00:27:57,392
Sir , we can change things . We can make things better . You know that .

393
00:27:57,551 --> 00:27:59,929
We are on the verge of undreamed-of discoveries

394
00:28:00,095 --> 00:28:04,942
if we only have the courage to ask the right questions . Now , you must help me . Please

395
00:28:07,352 --> 00:28:09,446
Come on .

396
00:28:09,605 --> 00:28:12,654
Victor ... VICTOR : Come on .

397
00:28:12,858 --> 00:28:14,860
[ III ]

398
00:28:20,782 --> 00:28:22,409
Henry -

399
00:28:36,423 --> 00:28:38,096
Lock the door .

400
00:28:43,513 --> 00:28:45,686
Now , for thousands of years

401
00:28:45,891 --> 00:28:48,986
the Chinese have based their medical science on the belief

402
00:28:49,144 --> 00:28:53,320
that the human body is a chemical engine run by energy streams .

403
00:28:53,482 --> 00:28:54,984
VICTOR : That 's fascinating . Then how do they explain- - ?

404
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:57,403
Don 't touch that !

405
00:28:58,695 --> 00:29:00,663
Their doctors treat patients

406
00:29:00,822 --> 00:29:03,996
by inserting needles like these into the flesh

407
00:29:04,159 --> 00:29:07,504
at various key points , to manipulate these electric streams .

408
00:29:07,663 --> 00:29:08,835
I see .

409
00:29:08,997 --> 00:29:11,500
So electricity is the key .

410
00:29:11,833 --> 00:29:15,178
Now , look at this .

411
00:29:17,923 --> 00:29:19,925
[ III ]

412
00:29:26,348 --> 00:29:28,350
[ BOTH GASP ]

413
00:29:29,184 --> 00:29:31,437
Go on , touch it .

414
00:29:35,691 --> 00:29:38,035
It feels warm . It is .

415
00:29:39,569 --> 00:29:42,197
Yes . How do you do ?

416
00:29:43,865 --> 00:29:46,084
Aah ! Turn it off !

417
00:29:46,243 --> 00:29:48,587
I can 't , it 's not working . Try to stay calm , Henry .

418
00:29:48,745 --> 00:29:51,168
It 's simply a matter of reducing the polarity in your body 0r in the arm .

419
00:29:51,331 --> 00:29:53,504
A monkey 's arm is basically the same as a human being .

420
00:29:53,667 --> 00:29:55,544
No arm is this strong ! Now , this must work .

421
00:29:55,711 --> 00:29:56,928
[ ELECTRICTY BUZZES ]

422
00:30:03,385 --> 00:30:06,355
Let me help you , professor .

423
00:30:08,223 --> 00:30:10,521
You shall , of course , tell no one .

424
00:30:12,269 --> 00:30:15,113
They wouldn 't believe you anyway .

425
00:30:20,402 --> 00:30:25,374
Dearest Victor . Nothing much changes here .

426
00:30:25,866 --> 00:30:31,088
Mrs. Moritz continues to love and torment Justine , in equal measure .

427
00:30:31,246 --> 00:30:33,214
Willie grows more precocious every day ,

428
00:30:33,373 --> 00:30:35,375
and Father almost expires with pride

429
00:30:35,542 --> 00:30:37,590
at the very thought of you and your work .

430
00:30:37,753 --> 00:30:39,255
And I ...

431
00:30:39,421 --> 00:30:44,393
Well , I just miss you , very much .

432
00:30:44,634 --> 00:30:46,636
Please write soon , Victor .

433
00:30:47,304 --> 00:30:49,898
VICTOR : ' No , I 'm serious . You take vaccine , for instance .

434
00:30:50,057 --> 00:30:53,106
Thirty years ago the entire concept of vaccine was unheard of

435
00:30:53,268 --> 00:30:55,145
and now we save lives every day .

436
00:30:55,312 --> 00:30:57,815
But that isn 't the whole answer . What do you mean ?

437
00:30:58,023 --> 00:31:01,948
That sooner or later the best way to cheat death will be to create life .

438
00:31:02,110 --> 00:31:03,657
HEN RY : Now you 've gone too far .

439
00:31:03,820 --> 00:31:06,744
There 's only one God , Victor . No , leave God out of this .

440
00:31:06,907 --> 00:31:09,456
Listen , if you loved someone , they had a sick heart ,

441
00:31:09,618 --> 00:31:10,835
wouldn 't you give them a healthy one ?

442
00:31:10,994 --> 00:31:12,587
Impossible . VICTOR : No , ifs not impossible .

443
00:31:12,746 --> 00:31:13,838
We can do it , we 're steps away .

444
00:31:13,997 --> 00:31:17,422
And if we can do that- - If we can replace one part of a human being , we can replace every part .

445
00:31:17,584 --> 00:31:19,757
And if we do that , we can design a life .

446
00:31:19,920 --> 00:31:22,844
We can create a being that will not grow old or sicken .

447
00:31:23,048 --> 00:31:25,301
One that will be stronger than us , better than us .

448
00:31:25,467 --> 00:31:28,016
One that will be more intelligent than us , more civilized than us .

449
00:31:28,178 --> 00:31:31,182
In our lifetime ? No .

450
00:31:32,099 --> 00:31:34,101
[ III ]

451
00:31:35,310 --> 00:31:37,984
How close did you get , professor ' ?

452
00:31:38,146 --> 00:31:39,363
Too close .

453
00:31:42,818 --> 00:31:45,037
Professor , I beg you , let me see these notes .

454
00:31:45,195 --> 00:31:47,823
No . My work now , and its application ,

455
00:31:47,989 --> 00:31:51,960
lies exclusively in the preservation of life .

456
00:31:52,119 --> 00:31:55,214
I abandoned my other researches many years ago .

457
00:31:55,372 --> 00:31:56,464
Why ?

458
00:31:58,291 --> 00:32:01,386
Because they resulted in abomination .

459
00:32:01,586 --> 00:32:03,588
[ WOMAN SCREAMING ]

460
00:32:03,755 --> 00:32:05,757
[ PEOPLE SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY ]

461
00:32:21,314 --> 00:32:24,739
You 're not sticking that in me . It 's got a pox in it , I hear .

462
00:32:24,901 --> 00:32:26,494
Pox ? They 've given us pox ? That 's right . Pox .

463
00:32:26,653 --> 00:32:29,873
It 's not pox , it 's a vaccine that will prevent a plague in this city .

464
00:32:30,031 --> 00:32:32,375
What 's that ? It 's a tiny , harmless amount

465
00:32:32,534 --> 00:32:35,162
of anti-smallpox serum . You just said pox !

466
00:32:35,328 --> 00:32:36,830
WALDMAN : I said it was harmless .

467
00:32:36,997 --> 00:32:40,251
It 's a necessary precaution , without which this godforsaken city

468
00:32:40,417 --> 00:32:42,590
would be immediately put under quarantine .

469
00:32:42,752 --> 00:32:46,552
You doctors kill people . I don 't care what you say . You 're not sticking that in me .

470
00:32:46,715 --> 00:32:48,717
Yes , I am . It 's the law !

471
00:32:48,884 --> 00:32:51,512
Sit him down , someone . Come on .

472
00:32:51,678 --> 00:32:55,148
You 're not sticking that in me !

473
00:32:55,557 --> 00:32:56,729
[ GRUNTS ]

474
00:32:56,892 --> 00:33:00,146
Sir ? Professor ? Sir ?

475
00:33:00,312 --> 00:33:02,064
[ SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY AND WOMEN SCREAMING ]

476
00:33:02,230 --> 00:33:03,903
Find him !

477
00:33:04,900 --> 00:33:08,404
Come on ! Come on ! Come on !

478
00:33:09,029 --> 00:33:10,406
It 's no use , Victor , he 's gone .

479
00:33:10,572 --> 00:33:12,415
No ! No , Henry ! Let him go !

480
00:33:12,574 --> 00:33:16,249
No ! No , this shouldn 't happen ! Let him go ! Victor , stop !

481
00:33:16,411 --> 00:33:18,539
VICTOR : It shouldn 't happen ! HEN RY : Stop ! Victor .

482
00:33:18,705 --> 00:33:23,711
It need not happen !

483
00:33:26,213 --> 00:33:28,215
[ CROWD JEERING ]

484
00:33:30,383 --> 00:33:32,226
MAN : The hell with you !

485
00:33:33,303 --> 00:33:38,810
Whatever you say , whatever you call it , you doctors are killers .

486
00:33:39,601 --> 00:33:43,947
You murder people ! Evil ! You 're evil !

487
00:33:44,439 --> 00:33:45,816
Evil !

488
00:33:45,982 --> 00:33:52,331
You 're the ones that deserve to die . God will punish you . He 'll punish you !

489
00:33:52,781 --> 00:33:55,955
God will punish you !

490
00:34:00,622 --> 00:34:02,624
[ CHEERING ]

491
00:34:10,298 --> 00:34:14,974
My God , you were so close ! Of course , the power !

492
00:34:15,136 --> 00:34:19,812
The materials were wrong . You needed auxiliary sources .

493
00:34:19,975 --> 00:34:23,775
" The experiment a failure .

494
00:34:23,937 --> 00:34:29,819
Resulting reanimant malformed and hideous to behold .

495
00:34:29,985 --> 00:34:34,331
This factor dependant on the appropriate raw materials . "

496
00:34:39,119 --> 00:34:40,962
Raw materials ...

497
00:34:41,121 --> 00:34:43,123
[ III ]

498
00:34:44,416 --> 00:34:46,418
[ THUNDER RUMBLING ]

499
00:35:00,181 --> 00:35:01,433
VICTOR : Come on , Henry . HEN RY : I can 't , Victor .

500
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:02,977
I can 't help you . You won 't help me .

501
00:35:03,143 --> 00:35:04,736
What are you frightened of ? Everything ! What do you think ?

502
00:35:04,894 --> 00:35:06,020
And what if the authorities- - ?

503
00:35:06,187 --> 00:35:09,191
We 'll do this in secret . I 've got the raw materials , I 've got Waldman 's journals .

504
00:35:09,357 --> 00:35:10,825
Together we know more than Krempe 's whole staff .

505
00:35:10,984 --> 00:35:12,031
You stole Waldman 's journals ?

506
00:35:12,193 --> 00:35:13,866
We owe it to him to complete this work .

507
00:35:14,029 --> 00:35:16,202
He was one step away . He never wanted this .

508
00:35:16,364 --> 00:35:18,037
Couldn 't face it , there 's a difference .

509
00:35:18,366 --> 00:35:22,041
Even if it were possible , and even if you had the right- -

